        "content": "Project identification is the initial phase of venture creation where entrepreneurs systematically search for viable business ideas derived from unmet needs, market inefficiencies, or technological disruptions.\n\n### Ideation Frameworks in Agriculture\n- **Problem-Centric Ideation:** Pinpointing severe agricultural pain points (e.g., tomato post-harvest rotting leading to solar dehydrator development).\n- **Residue / By-product Valorization:** Transforming agricultural waste into high-value products (e.g., converting paddy straw into mushroom substrates or biodegradable packaging).\n- **Import Substitution:** Producing commodities domestically that are heavily imported (e.g., domestic cultivation of palm oil, pulses, or exotic mushrooms).\n\n### Opportunity Screening Criteria\nIdeas must be screened through a rigorous filter: (1) Market Size and Growth Rate, (2) Technical Feasibility, (3) Regulatory Clearance (FSSAI, CIB&RC), (4) Raw Material Seasonality and Perishability, and (5) Founder-Opportunity Fit (technical domain competence).",
