        "content": "A Detailed Project Report (DPR) is the comprehensive, bankable master document presenting detailed operational, engineering, financial, and managerial blueprints submitted to lending institutions for term loan sanctions.\n\n### Alexander Osterwalder's Business Model Canvas (BMC)\nThe BMC provides a visual, holistic one-page framework deconstructing a business venture into 9 interconnected building blocks:\n1. **Customer Segments:** Target groups the enterprise serves (e.g., health-conscious urban households, institutional food chains).\n2. **Value Propositions:** The bundle of products and services creating value for specific segments (e.g., residue-free, lab-certified organic pulses delivered within 24 hours of harvest).\n3. **Channels:** Touchpoints for communication, distribution, and sales (e.g., e-commerce app, farm gate kiosk, wholesale distributors).\n4. **Customer Relationships:** Types of relationships established (e.g., dedicated personal agronomist, automated subscription).\n5. **Revenue Streams:** Commercial cash generation mechanisms (e.g., asset sales, machinery leasing, subscription fees).\n6. **Key Resources:** Crucial assets required (e.g., climate-controlled polyhouses, germplasm patents, cold-chain reefer fleet).\n7. **Key Activities:** Critical operational actions (e.g., soil health testing, sorting/grading, algorithmic demand aggregation).\n8. **Key Partnerships:** Strategic network of suppliers and partners (e.g., local FPOs, KVKs, ICAR research labs, logistics providers).\n9. **Cost Structure:** Major monetary outlays (e.g., cold storage electrical power, raw material procurement, cold-chain transport, compliance).",
